Oracle guard for MerkleAdapter
├── when receiving an authenticated report
│   ├── when NAV exceeds the growth or loss limit
│   │   ├── it latches the freeze without changing accepted NAV, nonce or timestamp
│   │   ├── it emits only RejectReport with the cached report payload
│   │   └── it rejects subsequent reports until the guard role clears the freeze
│   ├── when NAV equals either percentage boundary
│   │   └── it accepts the report and advances the baseline
│   ├── when a movement limit is below one basis point
│   │   ├── it accepts a one-part-per-million move and rejects a larger move
│   │   └── it rounds a sub-unit allowance down
│   ├── when both movement limits are 100 percent
│   │   └── it accepts doubling NAV and a total loss
│   ├── when queued allocations enter NAV or withdrawals become reserved
│   │   └── it compares performance after reconciling those movements
│   ├── when uninvested allocations remain queued
│   │   └── it does not use that queue to dilute the percentage limit
│   ├── when the accounting baseline overflows
│   │   └── it reverts delivery and review without changing oracle state
│   ├── when report reserves overflow or are unfunded
│   │   └── it freezes without committing the report
│   └── when the baseline is zero
│       └── it rejects an unexplained positive NAV, including the first report
├── when a curator manages the guard
│   ├── it requires separate enumerable guard and limit roles
│   ├── it does not implicitly authorize the owner or default admin
│   ├── it checks oracle-local roles and applies revocations immediately
│   ├── it rejects limits above one million before narrowing full-width inputs
│   ├── it packs both limits with the freeze flag and preserves independent writes
│   ├── it keeps the freeze when policy changes
│   ├── it emits FreezeOracle without a report hash when freezing manually
│   └── when one exact report is reviewed
│       ├── it applies the latest authenticated rejection once without redelivery
│       ├── it rejects uncached future reports and clears the rejection cache on recovery
│       └── it preserves authentication, freshness and reserve checks
├── when NAV is frozen or stale
│   ├── it reverts NAV-dependent vault operations after the immutable age limit
│   ├── it keeps proven, role-authorized manage actions available for recovery
│   └── it does not refresh the NAV timestamp when clearing a freeze
├── when changing the accepted workflow
│   ├── it continues accepting the old workflow while its replacement is proposed
│   └── it reconciles queued allocations and withdrawals across the accepted cutover
├── when delivered by the real Keystone forwarder
│   ├── it records successful delivery but rejected NAV separately
│   ├── it preserves the freeze across subsequent reverting calls
│   └── it directly applies the cached reviewed report without a new CRE execution
└── when bootstrapping a new adapter
    ├── it creates adapter and receiver addresses with report acceptance disabled
    ├── it binds the reviewed workflow by provider proposal and curator acceptance
    ├── it keeps the same receiver and implementation version
    ├── it rejects NAV-dependent operations until the first accepted report
    └── it accepts a signed initial report without changing either address
